  "body": "### Issue\n\nafter 0.53 I started to experience following problem. If during refactoring aider decides to create a file or if I explicitly ask it to create a file, it generates `SEARCH/REPLACE`  for new file, but then doesn't try to create a new file:\r\n\r\n```\r\n> /code i asked to move bucket config to a separate file\r\n\r\nI apologize for the oversight. You're right, we need to move the bucket configuration to a\r\nseparate file. Let's make that change now.\r\n\r\nFirst, let's create a new file for the bucket configuration:\r\n\r\nterraform/renovate/bucket.tf\r\n\r\n <<<<<<<SEARCH\r\n =======\r\n resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"renovate-terraform\" {\r\n \r\n // omitted output\r\n \r\n Tokens: 6.8k sent, 812 received. Cost: $0.03 message, $0.07 session.\r\nApplied edit to terraform/renovate/role.tf\r\nNo changes made to git tracked files.\r\nNo changes made to git tracked files.\r\n```\n\n### Version and model info\n\nAider v0.54.4\r\nMain model: claude-3-5-sonnet-20240620 with diff edit format, infinite output\r\nWeak model: claude-3-haiku-20240307\r\nGit repo: ../../.git with 250 files\r\nRepo-map: using 1024 tokens, auto refresh\r\nAdded terraform/renovate/role.tf to the chat.\r\n",
